  "question": {
    "text": "Which one of the following compounds has the smallest bond angle in its molecule?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{OH}_2$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{SH}_2$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{NH}_3$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{SO}_2$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "In $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{~S}$, due to low electronegativity of sulphur the L.P. - L.P. repulsion is more than B.P. - B.P. repulsion and hence the bond angle is $92^{\\circ}$."
